<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices mixed at third winter sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices mixed at third winter sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Demand was mixed for different categories of mohair at the third sale of the winter selling season, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. Buyers favoured adult and young goat hair, while only limited demand was seen for kid hair. Of the 3,018 bales offered, 86 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2600-2872     (2600-2770)</p>
<p>		  medium     2350-2630     (1890-2650)</p>
<p>		  short	2422-2494     (2452-2522)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2530-3000     (2510-3500)</p>
<p>		  medium     2400-2600     (2470-2650)</p>
<p>		  short	2420-2692     (2470-2530)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 3350-6002     (3200-5092)</p>
<p>		  medium     2850-3702     (3000-5010)</p>
<p>		  short	2702-3450     (2800-3562)</p>
<p>The fourth winter sale of the season is scheduled for October 22, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
